    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:synchrotron",
      "title": "Hyperion Synchrotron",
      "text": "A ring accelerator built from real beamline parts: bending dipoles, focusing quadrupoles, RF cavities, cryogenics, vacuum pumps and a detector hall. It makes the exotic hadrons nothing else can.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Like the collider, but a real beamline, and every part matters:$(li)dipoles bend$(li)quadrupoles focus$(li)RF cavities accelerate$(li)cryo jackets keep the magnets superconducting$(li)pumps keep the pipe empty$(li)the detector hall sees what was made"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Why a ring: a magnetic field curves a charged beam, so the same cavities can kick it again on every lap. A synchrotron raises its field in step with the beam's energy - hence the name.$(br2)Better $(item)coils$() unlock heavier particles: $(item)Glueball Cores$() need tier 2, $(item)Hyperon Crystals$() tier 3."
    },
